title: "Practical NLP: a hands-on course in classical natural language processing"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hentabli
    given-names: Hamza
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9530-2815"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/practical-nlp-course"
url: "https://github.com/hentablihamza/practical-nlp-course"
abstract: >
  A hands-on, 12-notebook Jupyter course in classical natural language processing:
  text preprocessing, one-hot and Bag-of-Words, term frequency and TF-IDF, n-grams,
  document similarity, LSA, word2vec and GloVe embeddings, and classic machine-learning
  text classification with proper evaluation. Used for teaching Master 1 students at the
  University of Médéa (2022-2023). Every notebook runs in Google Colab and offline from
  cached data.
keywords:
